      ],
      "extract": "In the case of $\\{x_{1},x_{2},x_{3}\\vert y_{1},\\dots\\}$ the non-perturbative corrections can be represented by a 3 dimensional cube. The vertex $\\{\\}$ represents the perturbative part, ${\\cal D}^{\\{\\}}$, while each other vertex represents a non-perturbative correction $,{\\cal D}^{\\{1\\}},\\dots$. The oriented edges show non-trivial resurgence relations between them. The alien derivatives move in the corresponding",
